&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Canada Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$67,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$75,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;The AirCover team is charged with managing and growing the AirCover business inside of Airbnb. We have a responsibility to our community of Hosts and guests to be there when things don’t go exactly as planned with their reservations. We have a lot of work to do in the coming years and we are looking for someone who will help us manage all of the things that need to be done to deliver best-in-class services to our community.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;As a Vendor Manager focused on operational vendor support, you will own the end-to-end management&amp;nbsp; and performance of a portfolio of third-party partners that deliver critical operational services (e.g., third-party claims adjusting). Applying deep expertise in vendor management, SLA frameworks, and operational risk, you will exercise independent judgment across multiple sources of data to structure trade-off decisions, resolve complex and ambiguous problems, and hold vendors accountable to service, delivery, and cost outcomes for guests and hosts. You will operate with minimal oversight, act as a trusted advisor and resource to less experienced colleagues and internal stakeholders, and may lead vendor management projects or programs that shape how the broader function operates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the day-to-day management and performance oversight of an assigned portfolio of vendors within established team strategy and governance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead daily/weekly performance forums, synthesizing multiple sources of operational and financial data to diagnose root causes, structure trade-off decisions, and drive action planning and accountability with vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the escalation point for complex, sensitive, or high-risk vendor issues on behalf of guests and hosts, negotiating resolution and building consensus across cross-functional stakeholders, including at more senior levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the design and priority of the metrics and trigger/appetite framework used to monitor vendor performance; independently determine when performance issues warrant action plans versus deeper investigation or escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use judgment to resolve complex operational issues and recommend trade-offs using established frameworks and data inputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vendor invoice management and financial governance process end-to-end, ensuring alignment with contractual terms and driving process improvements that reduce recurring discrepancies in credits, incentives, and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead quality and calibration programs across the vendor portfolio, structuring action plans to remediate opportunities and coaching vendors and less experienced colleagues on quality standards and remediation approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a resource and informal mentor for less experienced vendor managers, sharing best practices and subject-matter expertise; may lead discrete vendor management projects or process initiatives with manageable risk and resource requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Sourcing, and Finance to shape contractual obligations and vendor process improvements, applying knowledge of industry best practices and the competitive landscape to identify what differentiates Airbnb&#39;s vendor program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to team culture, onboarding, and change-management efforts on a recurring basis, at times in a team-lead capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in vendor management, claims adjusting, or outsourcing management, with demonstrated experience taking on greater scope, leading initiatives, or mentoring others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record independently managing large-scale, complex operational vendors (e.g., call centers, TPAs) with minimal oversight, including experience navigating executive-level vendor relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with proficiency in Excel/Sheets, SQL, or BI tools (Tableau, Looker, Power BI), and the ability to synthesize multiple sources of data into clear recommendations and trade-off decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent negotiation, executive communication, and stakeholder-management skills, with experience building consensus and explaining sensitive or difficult information to senior audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SLA frameworks, budgeting, and contract management, including the judgment to know when to structure action plans versus escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in quality management, process improvement (Lean/Six Sigma), and change management, including designing and leading calibration or remediation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the competitive vendor/outsourcing landscape and ability to translate that awareness into recommendations that differentiate Airbnb&#39;s operational vendor program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience acting as a resource, coach, or informal mentor to less experienced colleagues, and comfort leading projects or workstreams with manageable risk and resourcing needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a state where Airbnb, Inc. has a registered entity. &lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.airbnb.com/&quot;&gt;Click here for the up-to-date list of excluded states. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;mailto:reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;We ask that you only reach out to us if you are a candidate whose disability prevents you from being able to complete our online application.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$156,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Airbnb: &lt;/strong&gt;​Founded in August of 2008 and based in San Francisco, California, Airbnb is a trusted community marketplace for people to list, discover, and book unique travel experiences around the world. Whether an apartment for a night, a castle for a week or a villa for a month, Airbnb allows people to Belong Anywhere through unique travel experiences at any price point, in more than 85,000 cities and over 191 countries. We promote a culture of curiosity, humanity, and creativity through our product, brand, and, most importantly, our people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of workforce metrics (SLA, shrinkage, occupancy, adherence, AHT, etc.) with an ability to incorporate insights into planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep execution on Queue management, while effectively communicating strategies, processes across Broader Airbnb team and our Outsourced Partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in information gathering, data collection with analysis, and reporting SLA performance to broader domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance reporting with strong footprint of WFM metrics, RCA with supported narratives using trends and current performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support site-level resources with real-time management of schedule adherence and analyze performance data to identify opportunities to operate more effectively and efficiently&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and empathetically around strategies and business needs; build trust and transparency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter/Teamwork abilities: Workforce analyst must be able to work independently as well as function effectively as a member of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle dynamic situations: They require the ability to work effectively in a fast-pace situation and to handle multi-dimensional work, as well as to adapt to rapid changes in information, process, direction, or immediate workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to succeed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-developed problem-solving and analytical skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years WFM experience with hands-on experience on Queue management, understanding of scheduling with ability to read data as trend analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable working as an RTA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive problem solver; able to see big picture and streamline current processes while planning for business improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator and relationship builder&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel to other offices nationally and internationally on occasion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work weekends and holidays as business needs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Genesys WFM or similar applications (i.e.,IEX, Tableau, Superset, Salesforce)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn &amp;amp; manage multiple technical systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of Excel and Google sheet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is inclusive of allowances and is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus or incentives, one or more equity programs, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;India Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;₹770,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;₹970,000 INR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise Operations Workforce &amp;amp; Vendor Excellence team at Airbnb increases the effectiveness, utilization, quality and impact of the Homes, Hotels, Services and Experiences on Airbnb using AI and people-powered operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Workforce Planning and Insights team works with both our Scaled Operations and our Revenue Operations teams to optimize our vendor footprint, plan our capacity needs, staff projects and improve the performance of our vendor teams. The work of our agents is highly variable, from Sales work, to Account Management to AI labeling, often across 5-6 languages. We typically have 30-40 projects running concurrently, with demand changing weekly, so forecasting and staffing is a complex challenge. Our team moves very quickly, staffing up and down projects in the space of days, and increasingly uses AI as a core component of our workflows, which further speeds up cycle times.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;As the Workforce Management Lead,&amp;nbsp; Enterprise Ops, you will serve as the operational intelligence and capacity strategy hub for our Scaled and Revenue Operations teams. This is a high-impact, high-visibility role that sits at the intersection of workforce strategy, financial efficiency, and executive stakeholder management. You will transform complex, real-time workforce data into clear, compelling narratives that drive decisions at the most senior levels of the organization, proactively surfacing what is working, what is at risk, and where intervention is needed before problems escalate. You will own&amp;nbsp; our capacity planning, staffing and agent prioritization processes and work with our vendor strategy and contracting team to ensure we have the right number and mix of agents to meet business outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead demand forecasting, capacity planning and utilization reporting across both the Scaled Ops team and the Rev Ops Sales teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tightly run and improve our weekly project staffing and scheduling process, deciding the optimal allocation of agents across new and existing projects, including prioritization and trade-off discussions with multiple stakeholders, managing their expectations around balancing priorities and when to start, stop and continue projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a real-time, comprehensive view of all active and pipeline projects including tracking status, performance, blockers and distill this into a weekly / monthly executive briefing that gives senior leaders a clear picture of operational health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build consensus and secure decisions around program resources and requirements such as tooling, analytics and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our stakeholders to proactively build our project pipeline to ensure that the team has a strong bench of valuable work to transition to if other projects wind down early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure and report out on the team’s cost efficiency, including gains from e.g. the introduction of AI tools. Collaborate on quarterly OKR targets, and analyze the overall ROI of our workflows and motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the project governance system, ensuring that we work on only the highest value projects, and constantly review whether existing work should be continued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and escalate operational risks including capacity shortfalls, underperforming vendors, or misaligned project KPIs with a recommended course of action before they become critical issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on driving partner efficiency performance via a data-driven assessment of team and individual output, perform deep dives (such as time and motion studies), and structure the best measurements and incentives to optimize performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of operations experience in a fast paced and ambiguous work environment, with at least 5 years of experience in vendor management, workforce management and/or capacity planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience of influencing and managing stakeholders, including clear examples of negotiating difficult demands and mediating competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating as a strategic thought partner to senior leaders, translating ambiguous business goals into concrete workforce plans with measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong process design and execution skills; for example rebuilding and launching a new complex cross-functional process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience building capacity plans, staffing/scheduling plans, and allocating resources across multiple competing priorities based on ROI or alignment with company goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, ability to break performance out into underlying drivers and understand program ROI by taking a holistic view to costs and benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in Google sheets, should be expert at using complex formulas and should be able to create well-organized spreadsheets with raw data inputs. Experience with SQL is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving efficiency with onshore and offshore BPO partners for Quality, Trust, Sales or CS teams. The ideal candidate will have experience of both CS / back-office operations and Sales operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience introducing AI and automation to vendor workflows to drive efficiency and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated strong attention to detail and sound judgement in ambiguous situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leading large scale, high impact, cross-functional efforts and driving projects from ideation to strategy and implementation at the executive level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and running governance frameworks (e.g., portfolio review cadences, project intake processes, escalation protocols) that create clarity and accountability across a large, dynamic project portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and oral communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The candidate should be comfortable working in a remote environment and be able to independently manage their productivity based on performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep connection to Airbnb’s mission and passion for creating Connection and Belonging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is Canada - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a province where Airbnb Canada, Inc. has a registered entity. Currently we can hire in the following provinces: Ontario, British Columbia, Quebec, and Saskatchewan. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with your recruiter on what provinces you are eligible to work from.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We ask that you only reach out to us if you are a candidate whose disability prevents you from being able to complete our online application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We use automated tools to help our recruiting team efficiently screen a large volume of applications. All final hiring decisions are made by a human reviewer.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;This role is newly created and does not replace or backfill an existing position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Canada Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$128,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Management team at Bridge is dedicated to the growth, retention, and expansion of key customers. Our Scaled Account Management team focuses on driving measurable expansion across a broad portfolio of mid-market and high-growth customers through data-driven strategies, efficient processes, and strong cross-functional partnership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Scaled Account Manager at Bridge you will own a book of existing accounts and be responsible for expanding revenue, identifying product gaps and driving product adoption, preventing churn and ensuring renewals at scale. You will combine consultative selling with volume playbooks, prioritization based on quantitative signals, and hands-on execution to identify and close upsell opportunities across your territory. As Bridge continues to develop within Stripe’s Money Management organization, you will also drive your customers’ adoption of additional features available through Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Own a book of existing accounts and drive revenue growth through additional usage, upsells, cross-sells, and renewals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Develop and execute scalable go-to-market strategies that increase revenue per account and accelerate product adoption across your portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Use data and quantitative analysis to prioritize accounts and identify the highest-impact expansion opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Generate leads through targeted outreach, research, and campaign execution; manage high-velocity deal cycles from qualification to close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Build strong relationships with customer stakeholders to understand business priorities, surface pain points, and tailor Bridge solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Lead commercial negotiations and renewals to expand and retain customer revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify churn signals in your book and implement strategies to prevent revenue losses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Coordinate with product, success, risk, and operations teams to solve complex customer needs and ensure a great user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Translate customer feedback into actionable product and process improvements to better serve scaled customer segments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-5–8 years of full sales cycle or account management experience focused on existing business accounts; experience managing a large book of accounts or high-velocity portfolio strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong analytical skills with experience using data to prioritize accounts, build business cases, and track outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Comfortable understanding technical product requirements and articulating solutions across multiple technology products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Demonstrated ability to close upsell opportunities and manage complex pricing or commercial negotiations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Excellent operational acumen and proven ability to manage time and prioritize across a high-volume territory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Highly motivated, persistent, and effective in ambiguous, fast-paced environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Superior written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Willingness and ability to work in-office in New York or San Francisco at least three days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Previous experience at a high-growth payments, fintech, crypto, or technology company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience with CRM tools, Excel, and basic SQL or a demonstrated comfort with data tools and analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Background in working cross-functionally with product, risk, and operations teams to deliver outcomes for customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Bridge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a team that values clear thinking, quantitative rigor, and customer obsession. At Bridge you’ll own meaningful customer outcomes, operate with autonomy, and have the opportunity to shape how we scale revenue across high-potential accounts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Management team at Bridge is dedicated to the growth, retention, and expansion of key customers. Our Enterprise Account Management team focuses on driving measurable expansion across a portfolio of strategic enterprise customers through deep account knowledge, flawless technical execution and strong cross-functional partnership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Bridge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a team that values clear thinking, quantitative rigor, and customer obsession. At Bridge you’ll own meaningful customer outcomes, operate with autonomy, and have the opportunity to shape how we scale revenue across high-potential accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Manager at Bridge you will own a book of existing Enterprise and Strategic accounts and be responsible for deepening relationships, expanding revenue, identifying product gaps and driving product adoption, preventing churn and securing long-term renewals. Specifically, we’re looking for someone who can execute on long-term sales strategies, engage with internal and external stakeholders, align on technical and business requirements with product teams, build value in competitive situations, lead commercial negotiations, and close deals. As Bridge continues to develop within Stripe’s Money Management organization, you will also drive your customers’ adoption of additional features available through Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop account plans and cross sell into your list of strategic customers, driving growth through expansion and new revenue streams&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations for large, complex renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders within your book of business, deeply understanding problems they are solving and helping drive to solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Be responsible for account mapping and coordinating effective meetings with the appropriate external stakeholders expanding the customer relationship&lt;/li&gt;
